+<script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"What is a seller net sheet?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A list of every line on your side of the closing. It starts with the price, takes off the payoff and your costs, and adds or takes off the tax split. The $350,000 example at the top of this page is one."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Who pays title insurance in South Carolina?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"On the state REALTORS association's standard contract, the buyer pays both title insurance policies, the owner's and the lender's. Buyer and seller can agree to something else in writing."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How much are deed stamps in South Carolina, and who pays them?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"$1.85 for each $500 of the price, and the seller owes them. On a $350,000 sale they come to $1,295."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Does the seller need an attorney in South Carolina?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Every South Carolina home closing must be supervised by a South Carolina attorney. If the buyer has a loan for a home they will live in, the buyer chooses the closing attorney. That attorney does not advise you, and your own attorney is a seller's cost on the standard contract."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I sell my house before my mortgage is paid off?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. The payoff is paid at closing from the sale money, and you keep what is left."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is the commission always 6 percent?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. Agents' fees are negotiable, and no law fixes them. On a $350,000 home, each 1 percent is $3,500."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How do I avoid wire fraud at closing?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Never follow wiring instructions in an email. Confirm them by phone with the attorney's office, at a number you agreed on in advance."}}]}</script>
