losing under form I-290. It is a prepayment of tax, not an extra tax, and you settle the real amount on your return. Check the box in the calculator above and it reminds you on your results.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;">The rates, the primary-home exclusion, and worked examples live on our <a href="/sell/capital-gains/" style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none">capital gains and withholding page</a>.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">Netting more</p><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;letter-spacing:-.01em">Three ways sellers net more</h2><ul style="list-style:none;display:grid;gap:.7rem;margin:1.4rem 0 0;padding:0;max-width:720px"><li style="display:flex;gap:.6rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.6"><span style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:700">&#10003;</span><span><strong style="color:var(--navy)">Price it right the first time.</strong> Homes that sit end up taking price cuts, and price cuts cost more than any fee. Our <a href="/sell/home-value/" style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none">free home valuation</a> sets the number from sold comps.</span></li><li style="display:flex;gap:.6rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.6"><span style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:700">&#10003;</span><span><strong style="color:var(--navy)">Spend on the small fixes.</strong> Paint, light, and decluttering routinely return more than big renovations. We tell you which is which for your house before you spend anything.</span></li><li style="display:flex;gap:.6rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.6"><span style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:700">&#10003;</span><span><strong style="color:var(--navy)">Reach more buyers.</strong> More qualified buyers means competing offers, and competing offers set the price. That reach is the core of our <a href="/sell/" style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none">listing marketing</a>. Selling on your own instead? Read the <a href="/sell/fsbo/" style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none">FSBO page</a>, including the coaching we offer.</span></li></ul></div></section><section style="background:var(--navy)"><div class="wrap" style="text-align:center;padding:3rem 1.5rem"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.9rem;color:var(--ivory);margin-bottom:.8rem">Want your exact net sheet?</h2><p style="color:rgba(244,239,232,.6);max-width:560px;margin:0 auto 1.6rem;line-height:1.7">Send the address and your payoff. We build the real one for your sale, free.</p><div style="display:flex;gap:.75rem;justify-content:center;flex-wrap:wrap"><a class="btn btn-primary" href="#lead-form">Get my net sheet</a><a class="btn btn-outline" href="tel:+18543332135" style="color:var(--ivory);border-color:rgba(244,239,232,.4)">Call 854.333.2135</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">Common questions</p><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;letter-spacing:-.01em">Cost to sell FAQ</h2><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.4rem 0"><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.5rem">How much does it cost to sell a house in South Carolina?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:680px">Plan for the agent commission, deed stamps of 1.85 dollars per 500 dollars of price, an attorney closing fee, a title policy, any HOA transfer fees, your prorated property taxes, and whatever you agree to credit the buyer. On most sales the commission is the largest line and deed stamps are second.</p></div><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.4rem 0"><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.5rem">What are deed stamps in South Carolina?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:680px">A state and county recording fee charged when the deed transfers: 1.85 dollars per 500 dollars of the sale price, about 0.37 percent. On a 300,000 dollar sale that is 1,110 dollars. The seller pays it by law and by custom.</p></div><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.4rem 0"><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.5rem">Does the seller need an attorney in South Carolina?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:680px">Yes. South Carolina requires a licensed attorney to conduct real estate closings, so the attorney fee is part of every sale, agent-listed or not.</p></div><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.4rem 0"><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.5rem">Do I pay capital gains tax when I sell?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:680px">Sometimes. A primary home usually gets a large federal exclusion, and rentals and second homes are taxed differently. Out-of-state sellers also face South Carolina withholding at closing. Our capital gains page walks through all of it.</p></div><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.4rem 0"><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.5rem">What is a seller net sheet?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:680px">A line-by-line estimate of what you walk away with: price minus payoff, commission, deed stamps, attorney and title fees, prorations, and credits. We prepare one free for your exact situation on request.</p></div><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.4rem 0"><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.5rem">Is the commission always 6 percent?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:680px">No. Commissions are negotiable and vary by brokerage and by listing. The calculator on this page uses an editable example so you can model any rate.</p></div></div></section>
